Reviewed external compatibility patch — amoebius Phase 1.

Upstream project: https://github.com/cr-org/supernova.git
Upstream channel: default branch (`master`); this patch is authored against the
  branch head rather than a frozen revision, so the resolver stays dynamic
  (`repository_layout_doctrine.md` section 4).
Applies to: `lib/src/Pulsar/Internal/Core.hs` in the `lib` subdirectory package.

Why the patch exists. GHC 9.12 removed the re-export of `Control.Monad.void`
that `Control.Monad.Reader` used to supply transitively, so the unmodified
module fails `-Werror` with an out-of-scope `void`. The patch adds the explicit
import and changes nothing else; it is a compatibility edit, not a behaviour
change.

Why not carry the fix elsewhere. Waiting on an upstream release would block the
whole pre-cluster band on a third party, and vendoring the entire `supernova`
tree to change one import line would replace a four-line reviewed diff with an
unreviewable source copy. The patch is applied by `cabal.project`'s
`post-checkout-command` into the run-local build tree; nothing under an authored
root is modified.

Review: the diff is reviewed on its own terms — the import it adds is the one
the compiler names — independently of the Phase-1 gate that consumes it.

diff --git a/lib/src/Pulsar/Internal/Core.hs b/lib/src/Pulsar/Internal/Core.hs
--- a/lib/src/Pulsar/Internal/Core.hs
+++ b/lib/src/Pulsar/Internal/Core.hs
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ import           Control.Monad.Catch            ( MonadThrow
                                                 , throwM
                                                 )
 import           Control.Monad.Managed
+import           Control.Monad                  ( void )
 import           Control.Monad.Reader
 import           Data.Foldable                  ( traverse_ )
 import           Data.IORef                     ( readIORef )
